{"pageid": 1421, "title": "Blumhouse", "revid": 2883, "categories": ["Production"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 300px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/9/9e/Blumhouse.png/revision/latest?cb=20251025014749\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Blumhouse\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/9/9e/Blumhouse.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300?cb=20251025014749\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"300\" height=\"150\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"Blumhouse.png\" data-image-key=\"Blumhouse.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a> \t \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:Blumhouse.png\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n<p><b>Blumhouse Productions, LLC,</b> is an American independent television and film production company founded by Jason Blum and Amy Israel in 2000. Through a ten-year first-look deal in 2014, many of their theatrically released films are owned and distributed by Universal Pictures.\n</p><p>The company is now home to both a <a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_(film)\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children (film)\">live-action film</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_(TV_series)\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children (TV series)\">animated television adaptation</a> for the  ongoing horror comic book <i><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_(comic_series)\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children (comic series)\">Something Is Killing the Children</a></i>, created by <a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">James Tynion IV</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Werther_Dell%27Edera\" title=\"Werther Dell&#39;Edera\">Werther Dell'Edera</a>, who wrote and illustrated the series respectively. All issues are published by <a href=\"/wiki/Boom!_Studios\" title=\"Boom! Studios\">Boom! Studios</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span></h2>\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/something-is-killing-the-children-movie-blumhouse-1236409897/\">Horror Comic ‘Something Is Killing the Children’ Getting Movie and Series Adaptations in Blumhouse Deal (Exclusive) - The Hollywood Reporter</a></span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></div>", "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T22:43:44+00:00"}